\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces What sets $\mathrm  {EIRP}_{90}$, and in which direction. The two-sided terms combine in quadrature to one interval applying to every limit; the signed terms are biases, stated with their direction rather than folded into an error bar. The channel response is carried by the injections rather than applied afterwards: at the ninety per cent point the recovered peak channel holds $1.93\times $ the nominal trigger, so the response is already inside the measured completeness and applying it again would count it twice.}}{9}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:p90budget}{{5}{9}{What sets $\mathrm {EIRP}_{90}$, and in which direction. The two-sided terms combine in quadrature to one interval applying to every limit; the signed terms are biases, stated with their direction rather than folded into an error bar. The channel response is carried by the injections rather than applied afterwards: at the ninety per cent point the recovered peak channel holds $\InjPeakAtNinety \times $ the nominal trigger, so the response is already inside the measured completeness and applying it again would count it twice}{table.5}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The result in five counts, each read from the rows of Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:ledger} so that the two cannot disagree. The line attribution is evaluated in the stellar frame at the adopted $\pm 50$\,km\,s$^{-1}$ half-width, and the last two lines are the spatial screen and the recurrence test applied in that order.}}{9}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ledgersum}{{6}{9}{The result in five counts, each read from the rows of Table~\ref {tab:ledger} so that the two cannot disagree. The line attribution is evaluated in the stellar frame at the adopted $\pm \MaskHalfKms $\,km\,s$^{-1}$ half-width, and the last two lines are the spatial screen and the recurrence test applied in that order}{table.6}{}}
